WEBVTT

00:01.340 --> 00:03.001
&lt;i>NARRAToR:
Previously on Two and a Half Men:&lt;/i>

00:03.175 --> 00:06.235
You were meant for each other.
What could come between you?

00:06.412 --> 00:08.573
- My sister.
- You got a sister?

00:09.181 --> 00:12.673
You know what, Herb? Judith can relax.
I'm gonna check into a hotel.

00:12.851 --> 00:15.183
Myra, no, you don't have to do that.

00:15.354 --> 00:17.015
Yes, she does.

00:17.189 --> 00:19.282
Hey, wait.
You don't have to stay at a hotel.

00:19.458 --> 00:22.188
- I got plenty of room at my place.
- Yeah, I'll bet you do.

00:22.361 --> 00:23.453
No strings attached.

00:23.695 --> 00:26.858
Why can't I sleep in my bed?
Aunt Myra's not there.

00:27.032 --> 00:30.468
I'm sure she will be. She's probably
just getting something in the kitchen.

00:39.111 --> 00:41.511
That's not the kitchen.

00:59.198 --> 01:02.531
Thinking of chewing your arm off?

01:04.203 --> 01:07.331
What? No, no, no. Why would I do that?

01:07.506 --> 01:10.134
I don't know, maybe because
you're not horny anymore...

01:10.309 --> 01:13.767
...and you just remembered
I'm staying through the weekend.

01:15.380 --> 01:19.510
Wow, you got all that from the twitching
of my shoulder muscles?

01:20.486 --> 01:23.148
I have those muscles too, Charlie.

01:23.322 --> 01:25.483
Okay, good to know.

01:26.358 --> 01:31.125
Well, to be honest,
I did have a momentary panic reflex...

01:31.296 --> 01:33.958
...but it passed,
and I'm actually happy you're here.

01:34.299 --> 01:35.664
You sound surprised.

01:35.834 --> 01:38.894
Surprised doesn't begin to cover it.

01:40.172 --> 01:45.041
Normally at this point in a relationship, I'm
busy plotting the appropriate exit strategy.

01:45.210 --> 01:46.507
For example?

01:47.112 --> 01:48.670
Well...

01:48.947 --> 01:53.611
...that would depend on whether I'm trying
to get rid of you just for today or forever.

01:54.753 --> 01:56.277
Let's say today.

01:56.655 --> 02:00.853
Okay, today I have to see my dermatologist
about a little rash.

02:01.426 --> 02:04.827
Oh, that's good.
All right, what about forever?

02:05.164 --> 02:07.962
Turns out it wasrt a rash
and they won't let me come home.

02:09.201 --> 02:11.465
- Impressive.
- Thank you.

02:11.637 --> 02:13.901
I'm kind of a savant.

02:15.707 --> 02:17.572
Looks like you're good at two things.

02:17.876 --> 02:18.900
What's the other one?

02:24.149 --> 02:25.980
- Oh, right.
- The piano.

02:35.694 --> 02:38.720
Okay, I just checked.
No one slept in my bed all night.

02:38.897 --> 02:40.728
None of your business who slept where.

02:40.899 --> 02:44.232
Excuse me, but if who sleeps in my bed
is not my business, then what is?

02:44.403 --> 02:46.132
Let it go, Goldilocks.

02:46.838 --> 02:48.669
- Morning.
- Morning.

02:48.840 --> 02:51.240
And how many times do you have to get up
to go pee?

02:52.077 --> 02:54.671
- I wasrt counting.
- I was. Four.

02:55.847 --> 02:58.441
- One was to get a glass of water.
- There's your problem.

02:58.617 --> 03:00.175
Stop topping off the tank.

03:01.587 --> 03:04.420
- What's going on?
- I had to sleep in Dad's room last night.

03:04.590 --> 03:07.787
Uncle Charlie invited Aunt Myra to stay
in my room but it turns out...

03:07.960 --> 03:09.518
Got it.

03:09.695 --> 03:11.526
Well, do you think it's fair?

03:11.697 --> 03:13.961
Nothing about your uncle Charlie's life
is fair.

03:14.666 --> 03:17.134
Finish your breakfast.
We'll get you fitted for a tux.

03:17.302 --> 03:20.237
- Why do I have to wear a tuxedo?
- Your mother's getting married.

03:20.405 --> 03:23.499
- You're in the wedding party.
- Why do I have to be in the party?

03:23.675 --> 03:26.269
Your mother still thinks you're cute.

03:26.979 --> 03:28.776
- Morning.
Morning.

03:28.947 --> 03:30.278
Everybody get a good sleep?

03:30.449 --> 03:31.814
- No.
- No.

03:31.984 --> 03:34.680
So, Charlie, where's this house guest
I'm hearing about?

03:34.853 --> 03:38.880
Uh, gee, I guess she's probably
still asleep in Jake's room.

03:39.057 --> 03:41.025
Oh, please. You are such a liar.

03:41.960 --> 03:44.155
- What?
- Forget it, Charlie. We know.

03:44.529 --> 03:47.020
- You do?
We do.

03:47.399 --> 03:50.129
Okay, well, I got a good night's sleep.

03:50.769 --> 03:52.828
Probably because Aunt Myra
doesn't pee a lot.

03:56.642 --> 03:59.805
- Can I talk with you in private?
- Oh, come on. It's no big deal.

03:59.978 --> 04:02.310
I was in the middle of flossing
and suddenly there she is...

04:02.481 --> 04:04.346
...sitting on my bed...
- Ah-ah-ah!

04:05.817 --> 04:07.148
He doesn't need to hear this.

04:08.153 --> 04:09.745
Fine.

04:10.289 --> 04:13.156
Like I didn't hear enough last night.

04:17.429 --> 04:19.226
Okay. Uh...

04:19.398 --> 04:25.530
Let me just start by saying I applaud
the gusto with which you approach life.

04:26.004 --> 04:27.494
Thank you.

04:27.673 --> 04:29.265
That being said...

04:29.441 --> 04:33.036
...are you out of your freaking mind?

04:34.880 --> 04:38.043
- Beg pardon?
- You just could not control yourself.

04:38.216 --> 04:40.741
A female's in the house,
she must be mounted.

04:41.853 --> 04:44.947
No, it's not like that at all.
And why do you even care?

04:45.357 --> 04:48.019
Why? You ask me why?

04:48.694 --> 04:50.685
Never mind. Not important.

04:51.363 --> 04:52.887
I will tell you why.

04:53.065 --> 04:56.466
Because every time you rut
with any woman...

04:56.635 --> 04:59.604
...even remotely connected to my life,
I end up suffering.

04:59.771 --> 05:02.865
- Oh, that's ridiculous.
- Ridiculous, you say?

05:03.041 --> 05:05.601
All right, all right,
let's look at the record.

05:06.845 --> 05:09.939
- You slept with Judith's sister...
- Well, yeah, but...

05:10.115 --> 05:12.345
- at my wedding reception.

05:14.686 --> 05:16.813
All right, poor timing.

05:16.988 --> 05:20.583
You had more sex on my wedding day
than I did.

05:20.759 --> 05:23.227
That part's not my fault.

05:23.695 --> 05:26.562
Okay, okay, let's jump ahead.

05:26.965 --> 05:29.126
When Judith was divorcing me...

05:29.301 --> 05:32.737
...who seduced
and then abandoned my lawyer...

05:32.904 --> 05:34.895
...causing her to take revenge on me?

05:35.273 --> 05:38.902
- Now, hold on, that chick was nuts.
- I lost everything.

05:39.411 --> 05:42.244
Well, to be fair, you didn't have
that much to begin with.

05:48.186 --> 05:49.619
And now...

05:50.055 --> 05:53.081
...that Judith
is finally getting remarried...

05:53.258 --> 05:56.853
...and I can see the light at the end
of the alimony tunnel...

05:57.028 --> 06:01.965
...you decide, "Hey, why don't
I start humping her new sister-in-law?"

06:03.168 --> 06:06.137
- That is not how it happened.
- I don't care how it happened.

06:06.304 --> 06:10.104
I only care how it's gonna end.
And it's gonna end badly for me.

06:10.275 --> 06:12.766
How? Explain how.

06:12.944 --> 06:14.206
I don't know yet.

06:14.379 --> 06:16.108
That's always part of the fun.

06:17.549 --> 06:21.815
Trying to guess how your penis
is gonna bite me in the ass.

06:23.655 --> 06:25.555
Alan, you gotta believe me here.

06:25.724 --> 06:27.954
This is different. I really like Myra.

06:28.126 --> 06:30.151
Oh, you like all of them.

06:32.063 --> 06:33.553
And then you don't.

06:33.999 --> 06:35.864
What's gonna happen
when you get tired...

06:36.034 --> 06:37.626
...of this poor gi...?
Morning.

06:37.803 --> 06:39.293
- Morning.
- Morning.

06:39.471 --> 06:41.063
Boy, I slept great.

06:41.740 --> 06:46.268
- Jake's bed is really comfortable.
- Don't bother, he knows.

06:46.445 --> 06:49.380
Oh. Boy, I slept great.

06:49.548 --> 06:51.880
Charlie's a terrific lover.

06:53.819 --> 06:55.514
Oh, this one's gonna be bad.

06:59.724 --> 07:03.023
I don't understand
why I can't have the blue tuxedo.

07:03.195 --> 07:05.163
You're going to your mother's wedding...

07:05.330 --> 07:07.890
...not hosting a game show
on Telemundo.

07:08.066 --> 07:12.002
This from a grown man
wearing a green polo shirt.

07:15.607 --> 07:18.167
All the other men are gonna
be wearing black tuxedos.

07:18.343 --> 07:21.437
If the other men were jumping off
a bridge, would you want me to?

07:21.613 --> 07:23.513
If it'd keep your mother
off my back, yes.

07:23.782 --> 07:26.842
- I'll get the jacket.
- Thank you.

07:27.018 --> 07:29.145
Listen, this is a very big day
for your mother.

07:29.321 --> 07:32.415
It's important that you cooperate
and make her proud of you.

07:32.791 --> 07:35.259
I'm her son. She has to be proud of me.

07:35.427 --> 07:37.361
You think so, huh?

07:37.596 --> 07:38.858
Have you met my mother?

07:39.598 --> 07:40.724
Oh, yeah.

07:41.533 --> 07:43.057
Let me explain something to you.

07:43.235 --> 07:46.830
A womars wedding day is something
she will remember for the rest of her life.

07:47.005 --> 07:51.408
So if you screw it up, she will never forgive
you, even if it was your brother's fault...

07:51.576 --> 07:55.342
...and there was nothing you could do
to prevent it short of having him fixed.

07:56.248 --> 07:58.079
Don't worry, Dad. It'll be fine.

07:58.984 --> 08:01.214
- Thank you.
- I don't have a brother.

08:04.422 --> 08:08.552
Hey, listen, we haven't really talked
about what all this means.

08:08.860 --> 08:12.057
- What "what" means?
- Well, the big changes that are happening.

08:12.230 --> 08:15.893
It's just a couple of hairs, Dad.
It's not that big a deal.

08:20.505 --> 08:23.497
Not those changes.

08:23.909 --> 08:26.742
The wedding. You're gonna have
a stepdad in your life.

08:27.212 --> 08:30.511
- So?
- So is there anything you wanna talk about?

08:30.682 --> 08:32.411
Do you have any questions?

08:32.584 --> 08:34.916
- Just one.
- Yeah, buddy?

08:35.086 --> 08:37.247
Why can't I wear the blue tuxedo?

08:40.992 --> 08:43.517
Jake, your dinner's getting cold.

08:44.029 --> 08:46.361
So, what did you guys do today?

08:46.531 --> 08:48.396
We went on the Universal Studios Tour...

08:48.567 --> 08:51.263
...and then Charlie took me
to the Hollywood Wax Museum.

08:51.436 --> 08:53.529
You're kidding?
I thought you hate that stuff.

08:53.805 --> 08:55.102
What gave you that idea?

08:55.273 --> 08:57.901
Whenever I ask if you
to go someplace like that, you say:

08:58.076 --> 09:00.044
"I hate that touristy stuff. "

09:00.545 --> 09:02.706
- Well, this is different.
- How?

09:02.881 --> 09:04.940
I enjoy her company.

09:05.984 --> 09:09.784
And it's my first trip to L.A.,
so I wanna do all the traditional stuff.

09:10.088 --> 09:13.956
Tomorrow we're gonna sit in rush-hour
traffic and give other drivers the finger.

09:16.561 --> 09:18.426
Good evening.

09:20.966 --> 09:23.298
- Why are you wearing that?
- You said I look great.

09:23.468 --> 09:26.130
I don't want you messing it up
before your mom's wedding.

09:26.304 --> 09:27.532
I won't mess it up.

09:27.706 --> 09:30.470
Alan, you gotta admit he lends
a bit of class to the place.

09:30.642 --> 09:32.507
Thank you, my good man.

09:34.179 --> 09:38.479
Hey, speaking of the wedding, Charlie,
I have a favor I'd like to ask.

09:38.650 --> 09:41.483
- Sure.
- I have to be there and I was just thinking...

09:41.653 --> 09:47.319
...that the only way it is gonna be any fun
is if you come with me.

09:54.933 --> 09:57.834
You want me to be your date
at Judith's wedding?

10:01.172 --> 10:02.730
Yeah.

10:03.508 --> 10:05.066
We'll have some laughs.
What do you say?

10:10.782 --> 10:12.181
I'm laughing already.

10:14.719 --> 10:15.743
Uh-oh.

10:32.570 --> 10:36.404
Well, that's too bad, Herb. You tell Judith
if she wants me to be a bridesmaid...

10:36.574 --> 10:38.701
...and wear that brown satin
turd of a dress...

10:38.877 --> 10:42.973
...then I am entitled to bring whoever I want
as a date and I want Charlie.

10:44.683 --> 10:46.310
Okay, bye.

10:46.785 --> 10:48.377
See? No problem.

11:02.967 --> 11:04.628
Hi, Judith.

11:08.540 --> 11:10.167
Problem.

11:11.743 --> 11:13.335
Here's your suit.

11:13.511 --> 11:14.569
Thanks, Berta.

11:14.746 --> 11:19.046
The dry cleaners found $46
and a condom in the breast pocket.

11:19.317 --> 11:21.251
Here's the condom.

11:23.588 --> 11:25.886
Again, thanks.

11:26.057 --> 11:27.991
Can I give you some free advice?

11:28.159 --> 11:31.128
Free? I'm already down $46.

11:31.296 --> 11:34.925
What is it you say about going to a wedding
with a woman you're sleeping with?

11:35.100 --> 11:36.226
This is different.

11:36.401 --> 11:39.700
You say, and I quote,
"Better I should light myself on fire...

11:39.871 --> 11:41.600
...and run through a meth lab. "

11:44.109 --> 11:46.407
Oh, well, that's just a figure of speech.

11:46.578 --> 11:49.138
Come on, Charlie,
what are you doing with this girl?

11:49.314 --> 11:52.181
- What do you mean?
- I mean, she's a nice kid.

11:52.350 --> 11:53.715
You're gonna break her heart.

11:53.885 --> 11:56.149
- You don't know that.
- I know you.

11:56.488 --> 11:59.821
Myra's not one of your Handi Wipes
in high heels you can throw out...

11:59.991 --> 12:02.960
...after you wipe your Handi.

12:04.829 --> 12:06.922
You don't know
what you're talking about...

12:07.098 --> 12:09.760
...because this relationship
is not based on sex.

12:10.101 --> 12:11.796
Not based on sex?

12:11.970 --> 12:15.565
Well, unless she sweats bourbon
and farts hundred-dollar bills...

12:15.740 --> 12:17.765
...what exactly
is gonna keep you together?

12:19.611 --> 12:20.635
Oh, crap.

12:27.952 --> 12:29.180
No, you listen to me.

12:29.354 --> 12:32.414
If Myra wants to bring Charlie
to the wedding, that's her business.

12:32.590 --> 12:36.390
No, I will not intervene and you're just
gonna have to live with it. Goodbye.

12:37.629 --> 12:41.360
- I changed my mind. I'm not going.
- Oh, thank God.

12:43.701 --> 12:45.066
Judith, great news.

12:45.537 --> 12:47.471
I talked him out of it.

12:49.140 --> 12:51.404
- Hey.
- Hey.

12:51.843 --> 12:54.607
- What you doing?
- Grading tests.

12:54.779 --> 12:57.304
- Tenth-grade economics?
- Uh-huh.

12:57.482 --> 12:58.813
- Ask me a question.
- Okay.

12:58.983 --> 13:01.508
The functions and implications
of monetary policy are...

13:01.686 --> 13:03.483
Never mind.

13:03.655 --> 13:05.316
You sure? I grade on a curve.

13:05.490 --> 13:08.254
That's all right.
I'm stupid on a straight line.

13:09.861 --> 13:11.522
Listen...

13:11.996 --> 13:13.861
...about the wedding.

13:14.833 --> 13:17.427
I don't think I should go.

13:17.602 --> 13:19.035
Okay.

13:19.504 --> 13:22.996
I'm just concerned that maybe
we should slow things down a bit.

13:23.341 --> 13:24.399
What things?

13:24.976 --> 13:27.809
You know, things.

13:28.580 --> 13:30.013
I mean...

13:30.181 --> 13:32.649
...you don't know me that well...

13:32.817 --> 13:35.752
...and I'm afraid that I might hurt you
without meaning to.

13:36.955 --> 13:41.016
- Don't worry about it.
- Okay, good. I won't.

13:46.564 --> 13:48.555
Exactly what is it
I'm not worrying about?

13:49.467 --> 13:52.061
- Hurting me.
- Right.

13:54.439 --> 13:56.031
Why am I not worrying about that?

13:56.774 --> 13:58.867
I'm a big girl, Charlie.

13:59.043 --> 14:01.034
Some might even say a woman.

14:04.883 --> 14:07.283
I wanna go to the wedding with you.

14:09.120 --> 14:11.520
Don't worry about Jake.
I'll get him there in time.

14:11.689 --> 14:13.782
Well, you are very welcome.

14:13.958 --> 14:15.516
Best of luck to you and Herb.

14:15.693 --> 14:17.593
- Bye-bye.
- I'm going to the wedding.

14:24.435 --> 14:26.198
What is this, candle wax?

14:26.371 --> 14:28.839
How do you get candle wax on the seat
of your pants?

14:29.207 --> 14:30.970
- I don't know.
- You don't know?

14:31.309 --> 14:34.073
Okay, I might have lit a couple farts.

14:37.482 --> 14:40.610
- I'm ready. Myra's ready. Is he ready?
- Does he look ready?

14:42.253 --> 14:45.086
Well, he's not wearing any pants.

14:45.256 --> 14:47.554
That's ready for some things.

14:48.826 --> 14:50.418
Just go ahead. I'll get him there.

14:50.862 --> 14:52.523
Okay.

14:55.133 --> 14:56.794
What is that?

14:59.237 --> 15:00.499
Pudding.

15:20.558 --> 15:23.652
You know what?
I just realized something.

15:23.828 --> 15:26.820
I am two for two at Judith's weddings.

15:27.532 --> 15:31.195
What a coincidence.
I'm two for two at Herb's weddings.

15:31.369 --> 15:32.597
Huh.

15:32.770 --> 15:36.672
Okay, what about funerals?
Can you beat a three-way in a hearse?

15:38.776 --> 15:39.800
No.

15:39.978 --> 15:41.468
You have to think about it?

15:42.313 --> 15:44.406
It's a gray area.

15:45.683 --> 15:47.651
Where have you been?
I was looking for you.

15:47.819 --> 15:51.220
- We were having sex in the coatroom.
- Ha, ha. Good one.

15:53.591 --> 15:55.422
One of my groomsmen
got food poisoning.

15:55.593 --> 15:57.390
Walk down the aisle with Uncle Fred.

15:57.562 --> 16:00.156
Uncle Fred? Is that the only man left?

16:00.465 --> 16:01.762
Well, there's cousin Trudy.

16:01.933 --> 16:04.834
She's pre-op,
but she's wearing a very nice tux.

16:05.003 --> 16:06.937
Why can't I just walk down the aisle
with Charlie?

16:07.105 --> 16:10.506
Whoa, whoa, whoa. I'm just
an innocent bystander at this shindig.

16:10.675 --> 16:13.906
Oh, picture the look on Judith's face
when she sees you at the altar.

16:15.279 --> 16:16.769
I'm in.

16:17.348 --> 16:19.441
Oh, God.

16:21.686 --> 16:24.246
- Herb. Herb.
- Oh, hi.

16:24.422 --> 16:27.357
Thanks for bringing him down.
Oh, you look very handsome, Jake.

16:27.525 --> 16:29.755
I know. It's the tux.

16:29.961 --> 16:33.419
Okay, well, congratulations.
I wish you both a lot of happiness.

16:33.598 --> 16:35.896
- Thanks.
- Don't make the same mistakes I did.

16:36.067 --> 16:38.331
I won't. She wrote them down for me.

16:38.503 --> 16:39.868
Good.

16:40.038 --> 16:42.802
- All right, buddy, have fun.
- Okay.

16:44.675 --> 16:47.439
Oh, remember that tux is a rental.

16:48.913 --> 16:50.039
Excuse me.

16:50.381 --> 16:51.871
Are you Judith's ex-husband?

16:52.417 --> 16:55.443
Yeah, I was just dropping off our son.
I'm sorry, do I know you?

16:55.620 --> 16:57.554
Oh, no. Not really. It's...

16:58.156 --> 17:00.716
Herb and I were engaged
before he met Judith, so...

17:01.059 --> 17:03.960
- And you're coming to his wedding?
- Yeah, we're still friends.

17:04.362 --> 17:07.559
Well, how very California of you.

17:08.599 --> 17:10.464
Yeah. Well, I wish him the best.

17:11.936 --> 17:14.268
I have to tell you,
based on first impressions...

17:14.439 --> 17:16.600
...I'm not sure
that Judith is trading up.

17:17.608 --> 17:19.132
Oh, thank you.

17:19.310 --> 17:21.073
And having just met you...

17:21.245 --> 17:24.976
...I feel safe in saying that Herb's
not getting an upgrade either.

17:35.927 --> 17:37.986
Oh, man.

17:47.705 --> 17:49.502
- Nice dress.
- Bite me.

17:49.674 --> 17:52.905
Okay. Meet me in the coatroom.

17:53.077 --> 17:56.205
Listen, after the reception,
can you take me to the airport?

17:56.380 --> 17:58.610
- You're flying home tonight?
- Yeah.

17:58.783 --> 18:02.014
- I thought we had something going here.
- We did. Now I'm going home.

18:02.186 --> 18:04.552
Okay. Maybe I can come visit you
sometime.

18:04.722 --> 18:07.282
I don't think my boyfriend
would like that very much.

18:07.458 --> 18:08.618
You got a boyfriend?

18:08.793 --> 18:12.160
- He's more like a fiancé.
- You're getting married?

18:21.906 --> 18:23.897
Why didn't you tell me you were engaged?

18:24.108 --> 18:25.575
I thought it'd be awkward.

18:26.144 --> 18:27.975
Awkward?

18:40.958 --> 18:43.085
You may be seated.

18:49.000 --> 18:51.594
Mm. Oh. We really
shouldn't be doing this.

18:51.969 --> 18:55.063
- Why not? They broke our hearts.
- Yeah, but I'm kind of over it.

18:55.239 --> 18:56.433
I'm not.

18:57.909 --> 19:01.072
Hang on. Hang on. Hang on.
Maybe we can go out for coffee first.

19:01.245 --> 19:02.735
Or a movie.

19:04.382 --> 19:06.942
Alan, this is gonna happen with you
or without you.

19:08.786 --> 19:10.310
With me or...

19:10.488 --> 19:11.887
How does that work?

19:12.056 --> 19:15.514
The institution of marriage
is not one to enter lightly.

19:15.693 --> 19:20.528
So we pause at this time to consider
the depth of that commitment.

19:21.899 --> 19:24.959
SHANNoN:
Oh, Alan Harper, you animal.

19:25.369 --> 19:28.634
I can't believe Judith let you go.

19:28.806 --> 19:31.639
Oh, God, Alan Harper. Oh, God.

19:31.809 --> 19:37.611
Oh, don't stop, Alan Harper.
Please don't stop.

19:37.782 --> 19:41.115
Oh, Alan Harper.
I feel like a woman again.

19:44.422 --> 19:46.390
I'm Alan Harper, and I'm not having sex.

19:56.500 --> 19:58.900
- Hey.
- Hey.

19:59.070 --> 20:01.095
How was the reception?

20:03.174 --> 20:05.904
Kind of a letdown after the ceremony.

20:08.379 --> 20:12.315
But you'll be happy to know your
little outburst is already on YouTube.

20:13.584 --> 20:15.950
Damn camera phones.

20:16.821 --> 20:19.688
- Boy, is Mom mad at you.
- Yeah.

20:20.324 --> 20:23.418
She might start her second marriage
the same way as the first.

20:25.062 --> 20:26.620
So, ahem...

20:26.797 --> 20:28.025
...drinking in the dark, eh?

20:28.633 --> 20:31.227
It wasrt dark when I started.

20:32.970 --> 20:36.462
- Did you get Myra to the airport?
- Yep.

20:36.674 --> 20:37.971
And you know what?

20:38.175 --> 20:39.767
I'll never see her again.

20:39.944 --> 20:42.105
I was just a meaningless fling
to that girl.

20:43.848 --> 20:48.182
Huh. I'll bet this is that whole
karma thing people talk about.

20:49.353 --> 20:50.513
Could be.

20:52.556 --> 20:54.888
You know that feeling you get when...

20:55.059 --> 20:57.152
...somebody's gone from your life...

20:57.328 --> 20:59.455
...and you suddenly realize
that you miss them?

21:00.031 --> 21:01.521
Yeah?

21:02.733 --> 21:04.667
I don't care for it.

21:05.803 --> 21:07.964
Hey, you know what always
cheers me up?

21:08.139 --> 21:10.232
Pigs in a blanket.
